            "body": "Thanks for this. One adjacent problem in the same function that this PR could fix with little extra work:\n`_construct_message_from_response_item` reads only the first content part, so input items with\nseveral parts are silently truncated (the request still returns 200):\n\n- `ResponseOutputMessage` with `[output_text \"Part one. \", output_text \"Part two.\"]` → assistant content `\"Part one. \"`\n- assistant easy-input dict with `content=[{\"type\": \"input_text\", \"text\": \"A. \"}, {\"type\": \"input_text\", \"text\": \"B.\"}]` → `\"A. \"`\n- `ResponseReasoningItem` with two `reasoning_text` parts → only the first one\n\nJoining the text parts instead of picking `content[0]` covers both the multi-part case and the\nempty/refusal crash this PR targets, e.g.\n\n```python\noutput_text = \"\".join(\n    part.text for part in item.content if part.type == \"output_text\"\n)\n```\n\n(and `\"\\n\".join(part.text for part in item.content)` for reasoning, matching\n`responses/harmony.py`, which already joins all reasoning parts). Whether a refusal part should\ncontribute its `refusal` text is your call — I don't have a strong opinion. I left the summary\nfallback alone since #36516 deliberately de-prioritized it.\n\nHappy to send this as a follow-up instead if you'd rather keep this PR narrow.\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-17T22:20:20Z",
